// Chips' trees as its 0.13 board draws them, first captured from
// 846e17d753a157ecd0d4f2d143b92f4080123d01's hooks. Frozen: a change here must
// be justified in review, and is made by hand as CONTRIBUTING's "Chips' trees
// are frozen" says. Re-frozen in 0.18.0 for the rename to nextcost, and only
// for it: the footer says /nextcost, and the engine's hover `group` mark, which
// names the plugin, is no longer hashed. Before re-freezing, these trees hashed
// as the old ones once /nextcost and the plugin's name were read as before.
// Re-frozen again for the tests' project, /Users/me/workspace/nextcost, and only
// for it: every open view's strip names it. Read as the old claude-mod, each
// tree is the old one but in the strip: its hover cards span the shorter name,
// and at 40 columns the room it leaves keeps the parent folder whole, or the
// state.
// Re-frozen in 0.19.0 for two fixes, each alone: a text split bar fills its
// width exactly (the open cards on text surfaces, and the empty Text a zero part
// drew is gone), and the terminal's empty tracks take trackInk, which meets 3:1
// (dark terminal trees only).
// Re-frozen in 0.20.0 for one fix, and only for it: a cache write is priced
// by its lifetime, an hour's at 2x, so every re-warm on the pinned hour reads
// ~$2.44 where it read ~$2.13. Diffed whole, the ten trees differ in that
// figure alone.
// Re-frozen again in 0.20.0 for one wording, and only for it: a 5-hour pace
// cut short says `full ~1h`, never a bare `~1h` that beside the reset read
// as one, and the limit's hover ends `; full in ~1h at the current pace`.
// Only fiveHourAhead's trees move, in those two strings alone.

